00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.790
We begin with the not so pleasant Draugr,
and no these are not white walkers from game

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:20.790
of thrones if anyone was wondering.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:26.980
The Draugr are animated corpses or revenants
that can be found in burial mounds guarding

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.000
treasure.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.370
Step into the wrong tomb or try and steal
something shiny and you might just wake an

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.770
angry Draugr or two.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:41.280
In Swedish they are simply referred to as
Draug which refers to someone pale and dimwitted

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.280
who drags himself along.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.580
Given that description and the idea of animated
corpses comparing a Draug to a zombie is fairly

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:48.700
reasonable, they are also described as corporeal
ghosts and vampires.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:54.730
The zombie comparison can be made as it’s
said you can tell when a Draugr near as the

00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:01.680
smell of decay is unbearable, their appearance
is grotesque and necrotic.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:07.069
At times they can be gaunt with broken and
exposed bones.

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:13.000
Towards the end of the 19th century they were
also considered a type of vampire.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.970
Not because of the need to feed off others
in order to sustain themselves but because

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.630
their attacks could turn their victims into
their own kind.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:26.819
There are brief mentions of ‘outbreaks and
epidemics in the old sagas.

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:33.099
As Well as superhuman strength, they could
shapeshift, control the weather and even invade

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:40.220
one's dream leaving behind a cursed object
ensuring the victim's bad fortune and even

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.629
death.

00:03:41.629 --> 00:03:48.920
All of this makes being hunted by a Draugr
something you’d rather avoid.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:56.130
The Skogsraet in Swedish or the Hulder in
other parts of Scandinavia is a type of forest

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.130
nymph.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:03.829
Often referred to as the mistress of the forest
this entity is known for its seductive but

00:04:03.829 --> 00:04:05.389
also deadly nature.

00:04:05.389 --> 00:04:12.400
This mistress takes the form of a petite beautiful
woman with a kind and friendly demeanor.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:18.810
From the front they appear perfectly normal,
but from the behind they have a large hollow

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:22.720
Chasm in their back as well as a tail.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:28.470
Those unfortunate enough to interact with
these forest nymphs are never the same.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:35.750
Many are simply never seen again and the ones
who do return are said to be a shell of themselves,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.400
an introvert or hermit.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:44.130
Those who lay with the Skogsraet are said
to leave behind their souls for her keeping.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:51.680
One of the more disturbing set of creatures
on today's list are the Myling, these are

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:57.020
reanimated corpses or spirits of children
who had passed away.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:02.870
They are forced to roam the earth until the
dying wish has been fulfilled, normally that

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.710
means the desire for a proper burial.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:12.340
These spirits can range from young children
to newborns and even unborn children which

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.590
makes this legend even more disturbing.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:22.370
The Myling exists when a mother kills an unwanted
child and hides her crime, they can be heard

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:28.270
at night singing their horrifying song revealing
their mothers crime.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:35.419
With many of these murders happening shortly
after birth these children were never baptised

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:41.580
or given a proper burial thus according to
the church they could never rest.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:47.389
The way to appease them is by giving them
a name, finding their corpse and burying them

00:05:47.389 --> 00:05:49.580
in holy soil.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:56.000
Because of the violent nature of their deaths
the Myling were feared and considered vengeful

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:02.120
spirits, if you were chosen by a Myling to
help them find their body and bury them you

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:08.340
had no real choice, failing to do so would
result in your own death.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:14.740
The Nacken were water spirits that lured children
and women down lakes and rivers with enchanting

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.800
songs played on the violin.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:22.560
Often they appeared as a man with a violin
but it’s believed they had no true shape

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:23.840
or form.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:29.990
They could shapeshift into boxes of treasure
floating on the water's surface, a beautiful

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:33.129
woman or even an animal.

00:06:33.129 --> 00:06:39.030
A common form was a horse which is why they
may also be referred to as brook horse or

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.580
river horse.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:47.569
The most common form the Nacken spirit takes
in Sweden is a man playing a musical instrument

00:06:47.569 --> 00:06:51.500
who also happens naked sometimes.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:58.349
Not all Nacken were malevolent as there are
stories of them living on land and integrating

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:04.039
into society for short periods of time before
eventually returning to the water.

00:07:04.039 --> 00:07:10.479
There are also tales of Nacken teaching others
how to play the violin or fiddle but some

00:07:10.479 --> 00:07:14.110
are driven completely insane by the music.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:21.009
The evil Nacken would target unbaptised children
and pregnant women with their songs but they

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:25.849
also drowned young men too so I guess nobody
was really safe.

00:07:25.849 --> 00:07:30.290
The song played is so enchanting that you
forget where you are and begin walking towards

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:35.580
the music, before you know it you're in the
water about to drown yourself.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:41.439
Similar to creatures such as the Grindylow
or the Kelpie, these tales were likely created

00:07:41.439 --> 00:07:47.189
to keep children away from dangerous lakes
and rivers.

00:07:47.189 --> 00:07:54.280
The mare or mara is an entity that has appeared
throughout Europe under many different names.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:08:02.000
It is a spirit that rides on your chest while
you sleep and brings nightmares, a sleep paralysis

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.400
monster.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:09.139
The Mara would ride horses during the night
leaving owners confused as to why they were

00:08:09.139 --> 00:08:11.639
so tired and sweaty in the morning.

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:16.910
Once the horses were exhausted they would
find sleeping men entangle them with their

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:22.940
hair and begin to invade their dreams until
they became nightmares.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:28.020
As well as women they could also take the
form of any animal they desire making them

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.740
very difficult to identify.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:37.710
For our next sets of creatures I will now
